olling hash...\n\nStill computing hash rolling multiplication...\n\nStill working through the modular arithmetic hash computation...\n\nStill computing the hash...\n\nThat gives hex EE8A0624, so the resulting string is \"ee8a0624\". Now moving to string 6, \"Added alt text Improves accessibility\" — I'm computing the running hash and converting each character after \"Added \" into its numeric code for the next stage.\n\nStill computing the hash...\n\nContinuing the hash computation through more characters...\n\nStill computing the hash...\n\nContinuing the modular arithmetic to get a final hash value of 2159180538, then converting this result to hexadecimal digit by digit through successive division.\n\nI get 80b27afa as the hash, giving HDLmClass80b27afa as the class name. Now I want to verify this by re-checking the hash computation for \"Added \" since several other strings depend on this shared prefix, working through the multiply-by-33 and add-character-code steps manually.\n\nThat checks out. Now I'm continuing to verify the arithmetic for the second string's modular exponentiation, confirming the remainder calculation, then moving to double-check the hex conversion of 1480352102 digit by digit.\n\nNow I'm matching up the improvement descriptions—fixing a typo, adding a CTA button, meta tags, styling, hero heading, and alt text—with their corresponding hash values to build out the What/Why list.\n\nNow I'm assembling the full improved HTML, applying the generated hash classes to the specific elements that changed, like the typo fix and meta tags, deciding where to place classes that don't render visibly.I have enough context now, so I'll build the improved homepage HTML incorporating the six improvements along with their computed hashes.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I should grab that URL first.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"This is a basic list of links to Oz books, so I'll