es for the content.\n\nI'm planning six concrete improvements to log: fixing the typo, adding a hero headline, adding a CTA button, styling the book list, adding a meta description, and adding a footer—each paired with a brief rationale focused on trust, engagement, conversions, readability, and SEO. Now I need to work through the DJB2 hash calculation for each What/Why pair to generate the required identifiers.\n\nI settle on five short what/why pairs: fixing a typo for trust, adding a headline for engagement, adding a CTA for clicks, styling a list for readability, and adding meta tags for SEO. Now I'm working through the DJB2 hash arithmetic character by character for the first string, converting each letter to its ASCII value and folding it into the running hash.\n\nContinuing the hash computation through more characters, applying the multiply-by-33 and mod 2^32 steps repeatedly...\n\nContinuing the modular hash computation through h11, h12, h13, tracking each multiply-add-mod step.\n\nStill computing the rolling hash values...\n\nh20 finishes at 2466642397, and now I'm converting that value into hexadecimal digit by digit.\n\nWorking out the remaining digits gives 0x5F9DD, so the full hex value is 0x9305F9DD, which I verify by reconstructing it back to the decimal total. I'm using this to form the identifier \"HDLmClass9305f9dd\" in lowercase hex.\n\nNow I'm computing a second hash for the string \"Add headlineBoosts engagement\" using the same DJB2-style algorithm, working through each character's ASCII value and accumulating the hash step by step across all 29 characters.\n\nContinuing the hash computation through several more rounds, tracking each multiply-add-mod step for h8 through h11...\n\nStill computing hash iterations...\n\nStill computing hash iterations...\n\nContinuing the modular arithmetic, I get h29=2340561917, then I'm converting that value to hexadecimal by subtracting powers of 16 progressively.\n\nI confirm the hex result is 0x8b8223fd, givi